# ESP32-C5 only: ESP-IDF loads this after sdkconfig.defaults for IDF_TARGET
# esp32c5, so these lines override the shared 16 KiB, internal-RAM TCP
# configuration for the C5 DevKitC-1 and nothing else.
#
# lwIP pbufs and TCP segments, and the Wi-Fi driver's heap allocations
# (including its dynamic RX buffers), prefer the 8 MB PSRAM, so TCP windows
# stop costing scarce internal RAM. That pays for 96 KiB windows in each
# direction. Wi-Fi DMA buffers stay in internal RAM.
#
# A window over 64 KiB needs TCP window scaling, which ESP-IDF offers only
# when PSRAM is required at boot. At the ~100 ms round trip between a gadget
# and its VM, 64 KiB caps each direction near 5 Mbit/s: VM-to-gadget transfers
# ran at 3.2 Mbit/s with the CPU at 68%, and at 4.1-4.9 Mbit/s (median 4.7),
# CPU-bound, with 96 KiB (tools/coexist/README.md has the numbers).
#
# Requiring PSRAM costs two things:
# - PSRAM can fail to start on a power-on reset (sdkconfig.defaults). The
#   gadget now resets and starts again instead of running without it, and a
#   board whose PSRAM never starts doesn't boot.
# - The Wi-Fi driver switches to static TX buffers, allocated in internal RAM
#   at boot (about 1.7 KiB each). 4 instead of ESP-IDF's 16 hold the cost to
#   about 8 KiB of internal RAM; frames beyond them wait in a PSRAM queue.
#   4, 6, 8 and 16 measured the same through the tunnel, where the CPU is the
#   limit.
#
# The receive window needs a receive path deep enough to take a whole window
# in one burst: with ESP-IDF's 32 dynamic RX buffers and 4 queued
# out-of-order segments, a 64 KiB window lost segments about ten times per
# 4 MB transfer and VM-to-gadget throughput fell to 1.8 Mbit/s. 96 dynamic RX
# buffers (in PSRAM) and a 96-entry receive mailbox match 96 KiB. The
# out-of-order queue stays bounded (12 segments per connection, not ESP-IDF's
# "0 = unlimited"). The block-ack window stays at sdkconfig.defaults' 32.
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_IGNORE_NOTFOUND=n
CONFIG_LWIP_WND_SCALE=y
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_RCV_SCALE=1
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SND_BUF_DEFAULT=98304
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_WND_DEFAULT=98304
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_RECVMBOX_SIZE=96
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_DYNAMIC_RX_BUFFER_NUM=96
CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_STATIC_TX_BUFFER_NUM=4
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_OOSEQ_MAX_PBUFS=12
